<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Studenica Monastery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Studenica Monastery is a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-nemanja">Stefan Nemanja</a> around 1190 and his burial place. Its Church of the Virgin, faced with white marble, combines Romanesque and Byzantine styles and holds frescoes of 1209, and the monastery was the leading spiritual centre of medieval Serbia. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/studenica-monastery.jpg" alt="Studenica Monastery" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DjordjeMarkovic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manastir_Studenica,_Bogorodi%C4%8Dina_crkva_sa_ulaznim_portalom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
